    """Return the data of every ``<tr>`` row in ``html``.

    The result is a list with one entry per ``<tr>`` element found in the
    document, in document order.  Each entry is a list of the text contents of
    that row's ``<td>`` cells, in order, with tags removed, entities decoded
    and surrounding whitespace stripped.  ``<th>`` cells are ignored, so a row
    without any ``<td>`` yields an empty list.  If there are no rows at all, an
    empty list is returned.
