How it works:

- **Row detection:** Every `<tr>` start tag creates a row entry immediately, so rows come back in document order even in messy markup.
- **Cells:** Each `<td>` opens a text buffer; any text (including text inside nested tags like `<b>`) is collected into the innermost open `<td>` buffer. When the cell closes, its text is joined and stripped, then attached to the nearest enclosing row.
