The module is self-contained: it works with no third-party dependencies.
When the data is exactly representable (integers and simple dyadic decimals)
the system is solved in exact rational arithmetic, which yields clean,
exactly correct results for textbook inputs.  Otherwise NumPy is used when
available, and a pure-Python least-squares solver serves as the final
fallback.
